      "message": "`slugify(\"a--b\")` now returns `\"a-b\"`. `pytest tests/test_core.py` passes all 3 tests, including a new one for this case.\n\nThe fix is in `slug/core.py`. The function turned every non-alphanumeric character into a `-` without checking the previous output, so runs of separators stayed doubled. It now skips appending a `-` when the last character emitted is already one. That collapses runs of separators, and it also covers cases like `\"a-é-b\"` → `\"a-b\"`.\n\nI also added `test_repeated_separators_collapse_to_one_dash` to `tests/test_core.py` as a regression test. I did not change how leading or trailing separators are handled.",
